       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 15 g/day of acetaminophen is in the range that causes acute liver failure, and I can't think of a therapeutic reason for it. You also haven't given an indication. Entering it could seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere are some ways to go from here:\n- **Corrected dose:** Give me a dose within the safe range (maximum 4 g/day, or 1000 mg per dose) and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Unusual indication:** If there's a specific protocol or situation behind this, talk to pharmacy or toxicology first. If they approve it, it should go through the order-entry process that includes pharmacist review, not through me.\n- **Possible overdose:** If you're treating a suspected acetaminophen ingestion, the treatment is usually N-acetylcysteine, dosed by a nomogram. Poison control (1-800-222-1222 in the US) or toxicology can help. I can enter an NAC order if you give me the regimen."
      }
     ],
